# glow_desk_reach_witness.rish -- the desk witness's reach over the Glow desk corpus.
#
# Holds five readings at zero and one ratchet under a ceiling that only falls, over
# tools/fixtures/g/glow_desk_reach_scan.sh. The scan's own head carries the reasoning; the short
# form is that glow/gen/ holds 352 generated desks and exactly one guard runs any of them, by a
# hand-written enumeration of 218 that nothing derives and nothing measured until now.
#
# The fifth zero arrived 20260907.122532, when `covered` learned to read the derived runner beside
# the elder witness. For one lap the two answered differently about one population: the runner ran
# 301 desks on a roster while this reading called 83 of them run by nothing.
#
# The fourth zero and the second ratchet arrived 20260907.020441. The witness runs every desk it
# names with ZERO arguments, and tools/g/glow_run_worker.sh refuses an argument for any stem
# absent from its hand-written `case` -- so the 46 desks in this room that the worker WILL take a
# sample for are, all 46 of them, outside the witness's shape. Not one is covered. The elder
# single ratchet of 129 carried those 46 beside 83 desks that cost one line each, and a reader
# could not tell the two debts apart.
#
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/g/glow_desk_reach_witness.rish

let scan = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/g/glow_desk_reach_scan.sh"]
assert scan.ok else "glow_desk_reach scan failed: ${scan.err}${scan.out}"

# invariant: the corpus is present -- a scan reading zero desks has lost its subject, and every
# reading below would then be trivially satisfied by an empty tree.
assert scan.out contains "desks=" else "glow_desk_reach scan printed no desk count"

# invariant: the two run-contract markers name one set. A desk declares it must not run in its
# name and in its head; those are independent statements of one fact, and their parting is the
# silent drift this guard exists to feel. Held at zero.
assert scan.out contains "norun_disagree=0" else "glow_desk_reach: the name marker and the head marker name different desks -- a desk was renamed without re-declaring, or declared without renaming"

# invariant: every desk the witness names is a desk on disk. An assertion against an absent file
# proves nothing while reading exactly like proof. Held at zero.
assert scan.out contains "phantom=0" else "glow_desk_reach: the desk witness names desks that are not on disk"

# invariant: the witness never runs a desk that declares it must not run. When those two disagree,
# one of them is lying, and which one is a language question rather than a repair. Held at zero.
assert scan.out contains "contradicted=0" else "glow_desk_reach: the desk witness runs a desk whose own head declares it unrunnable"

# invariant: the worker's sample-permission `case` names files that exist. A permitted stem with
# no .glow anywhere in the tree is a dead branch -- the same fault `phantom` reads one enumeration
# over, and gated for the same reason. Held at zero.
assert scan.out contains "sample_phantom=0" else "glow_desk_reach: the run worker permits a sample for a stem that names no Glow file"

# invariant: `covered` reads BOTH instruments that run desks in this tree, and prints each apart.
# It read the elder hand-written witness alone until 20260907.122532, so it reported 83 desks "run
# by nothing" on a lap where the rostered derived runner ran all 83 -- two instruments answering
# differently about one population. The union is the answer to the question the reading's own name
# asks; the parts stay printed so the elder witness's own drift is still visible beside it.
assert scan.out contains "covered_witness=" else "glow_desk_reach scan printed no witness coverage count"
assert scan.out contains "covered_runner=" else "glow_desk_reach scan printed no derived-runner coverage count"

# invariant: nothing bare-runnable is run by nothing. This fell from a ratchet of 83 to a gate at
# zero when the derived runner landed and ran the whole bare-runnable set. Its character changed
# with its number: it is no longer a backlog counting down, it is the gate on two derivations
# agreeing. tools/fixtures/g/glow_desk_reach_scan.sh excludes by the markers' INTERSECTION and
# tools/fixtures/g/glow_desk_run_scan.sh by their UNION, so a desk half-declared reddens here and
# at norun_disagree together -- the truth said twice rather than once.
assert scan.out contains "uncovered_bare_ceiling=0" else "glow_desk_reach: the bare ceiling stands at zero -- a ceiling only falls"

# invariant: the sample-taking population only falls. Those 46 desks cost a judgment apiece --
# what argument proves this gate? -- and then a fourth hand-written enumeration to hold the
# answers, which is the shape %532 booked. A ratchet rather than a gate because the backlog was
# not made today, and a guard that reds on ordinary work is a guard somebody turns off.
assert scan.out contains "uncovered_sampled_ceiling=46" else "glow_desk_reach: the sampled ceiling stands where it was measured -- a ceiling only falls"

# invariant: the printed sum is its two parts added, never a third spelled number that could
# drift from them.
assert scan.out contains "uncovered_ceiling=46" else "glow_desk_reach: the sum ceiling must equal 0 + 46"
assert scan.out contains "verdict=ok" else "glow_desk_reach: the scan refused -- ${scan.out}"

# invariant: both refusal paths are reachable. A ceiling proven only in the passing direction
# cannot be told from a bypass, so the guard drops each ceiling one under its live reading in turn
# and requires the scan to refuse, naming each refusal apart from the marker gates and from the
# other ceiling.
# The bare gate stands at zero, so it cannot be proven by dropping the ceiling one further. It is
# proven instead by taking the second instrument away: a runner selecting nothing leaves exactly
# the 83 desks the elder witness never named run by nothing, on the live tree, and the gate fires.
# This is the reading as it stood one lap ago, made reachable on purpose rather than remembered.
# The pen is named from THIS TREE rather than written as a constant (REDS %549): eight ships
# share one pier and one /tmp, so a fixed name means one ship's sweep removes another ship's
# runner mid-read. `pwd | cksum` is stable across the four shells below and differs per ship.
let mute = run ["sh" "-c" "p=/tmp/glow-desk-reach-mute-$(pwd | cksum | tr -cd 0-9).sh; echo '#!/bin/sh' > $p; echo 'exit 0' >> $p"]
assert mute.ok else "glow_desk_reach: could not write the silent runner -- ${mute.err}"

let under_bare = run ["sh" "-c" "GLOW_DESK_RUNNER=/tmp/glow-desk-reach-mute-$(pwd | cksum | tr -cd 0-9).sh sh tools/fixtures/g/glow_desk_reach_scan.sh"]
assert (under_bare.ok == false) else "glow_desk_reach: with the derived runner silent, the desks it alone runs must refuse at a bare ceiling of zero"
assert under_bare.out contains "verdict=over_bare_ceiling" else "glow_desk_reach: want the bare ceiling refusal named -- ${under_bare.out}"
assert under_bare.out contains "covered_runner=0" else "glow_desk_reach: want the silent runner counted as covering nothing -- ${under_bare.out}"

# invariant: a runner that cannot answer refuses the whole reading. An empty selection and an
# absent instrument look identical in the arithmetic and mean opposite things, so the scan names
# the fault rather than letting a broken runner read as clean coverage of nothing.
let no_runner = run ["sh" "-c" "GLOW_DESK_RUNNER=/tmp/glow-desk-reach-absent-$(pwd | cksum | tr -cd 0-9).sh sh tools/fixtures/g/glow_desk_reach_scan.sh"]
assert (no_runner.ok == false) else "glow_desk_reach: an absent derived runner must refuse"
assert no_runner.err contains "no derived runner" else "glow_desk_reach: want the absent runner named -- ${no_runner.err}"

let sweep = run ["sh" "-c" "rm -f /tmp/glow-desk-reach-mute-$(pwd | cksum | tr -cd 0-9).sh"]
assert sweep.ok else "glow_desk_reach: could not clear the silent runner -- ${sweep.err}"

let under_sampled = run ["sh" "-c" "GLOW_DESK_UNCOVERED_SAMPLED_CEILING=45 sh tools/fixtures/g/glow_desk_reach_scan.sh"]
assert (under_sampled.ok == false) else "glow_desk_reach: a sampled ceiling one under the live reading must refuse"
assert under_sampled.out contains "verdict=over_sampled_ceiling" else "glow_desk_reach: want the sampled ceiling refusal named -- ${under_sampled.out}"

# invariant: the room can never again pass for the corpus. This scan's own door called glow/gen/
# "the generated desk corpus for the language" until 20260907.045422, while 99 of the tree's 451
# .glow files stood in five other rooms. corpus_glow and corpus_outside report and gate nothing --
# a desk landing in src/gate/ is ordinary work in another lane, and those rooms have their own
# runners -- so what they buy is a claim a reader can check rather than a sentence to believe.
assert scan.out contains "corpus_glow=" else "glow_desk_reach scan printed no tree-wide corpus count"
assert scan.out contains "corpus_outside=" else "glow_desk_reach scan printed no outside-the-room count"

# invariant: a stem held by two files is visible. The worker writes glow/bin/<stem> and matches its
# permission `case` on the stem alone, so two desks sharing a stem share one binary and one ruling.
# Reported rather than gated, since both of today's pairs predate the reading and which file keeps
# the name is a language custody question.
assert scan.out contains "stem_collision=" else "glow_desk_reach scan printed no shared-stem count"

# invariant: the reading itself is proven on real desk rooms rather than trusted. The control
# builds miniature desk rooms in a throwaway pen and plants each refusal, then lifts it --
# 81 behaviors, both sides of every gate and of both ceilings, and the two gates proven
# independent: a sample-taking desk refuses at its own ceiling while the bare ceiling stands at
# zero, which is the reading the elder sum could not express. The last of them is the one that
# earns the prune: a permission whose only file is a build-cache leftover reads phantom, where the
# elder spelling pruned .git alone and let the leftover keep the branch alive.
let control = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/g/glow_desk_reach_control.sh"]
assert control.ok else "glow_desk_reach control failed: ${control.out}"
assert control.out contains "fail=0" else "glow_desk_reach control reported failures: ${control.out}"

say "GREEN: glow_desk_reach -- markers agree, no phantom, no contradiction, no dead permission, covered read from both instruments as a union, zero bare-runnable desks run by nothing and 46 sample-taking at their ceilings, the room named apart from the corpus, both refusals proven, 81 control behaviors green."
